A calendar's own ``VTIMEZONE`` is now used for its custom ``TZID`` values, instead of a ``VTIMEZONE`` with the same ``TZID`` from a calendar parsed earlier in the same process. Previously, :meth:`~icalendar.timezone.tzp.TZP.cache_timezone_component` kept the first definition of a custom ``TZID``, such as ``W. Europe Standard Time`` or ``/freeassociation.sourceforge.net/Europe/Berlin``, so one calendar could shift the event times of every calendar parsed after it. I used AI to assist me with this change. @alhudz
